On Wed, 13 Jun 2001, Khangelani Zuma wrote:

> Hi there
>
> I would like to do a random sample from a Laplace Distribution using R. As
> far as I can see there is no function such as RBINOM, but
> for Laplace observations, in these packages. Is there anyway in which I
> can sample from a Laplace distribution using R?

Using R or using S?

A Laplace distribution is a two-sided exponential, so sample from an
exponentia, add a random sign and then shift if needed.

Is this a homework problem?  There is no standard function because the
Lapalace distribution is very uncommon in the real world.

