Message-ID: <443AF5CBFB7DD411AFA00000F8057A9F7CE826@sc002s.sc.dlo.nl>

Hi list,

Thanks to Bert Gunter, Nick Ellis, Ad Feelders and Victor Zurkowski for
their reactions.

Nick Ellis provided a solution that works if the dataframe contains only
which should be logical, numeric, or complex objects.

df<- expand.grid(1:3,4:6,7:9)
df[[1]][c(4,7,12)] <- NA
df[[2]][c(3, 12,9)] <- NA
df[[3]][c(15,6, 25)] <- NA
df
apply(df,1,function(x)any(is.na(x)))
df[!apply(df,1,function(x)any(is.na(x))),]

Bert Gunter provided the easy solution for any data-frame:

Use na.exclude() (see Help therefor). In older S-Plus versions, na.omit().

The apply() family of functions (apply, tapply, lapply, sapply) is available
for greater flexibility.

