Yes, that's the normal practice.  It uses ~/.Data where ~ is the home
directory, unless the current directory contains .Data. For versions 5.1
or 6.x, it used ~/MySwork unless the current directory is a valid chapter,
which includes containing a .Data directory but is more stringent.

Note, this is all about which .Data tree is used: the working directory
(for example where scan reads and dump saves) is the starting directory
wherever .Data is found.

