Hello Alison,

> 1.  I have tried hclust using the single, average and complete linkage
options  - the complete linkage method gives a good separation of the
clusters - but this is a subjective judgement.  How can I objectively test
which is the best method for the dataset I have using the SPLUS output?

I don't believe you can. In cluster analysis other than looking for the best
linkage method you should verify if the few linkage methods are coherent
using your data in order to have more robust results. Chatfield&Collins as
well as Johnson&Wichern are two possible good references for this.
Chatfield, C., Collins, A.J. (1980). Introduction to Multivariate Analysis.
Chapman and Hall.
Johnson, A.R., Wichern, D.W. (1998). Applied Multivariate Statistical
Analysis - Fourth Edition. Prentice-Hall.

Another questions is if your variables all continuous. Or you have a mixture
of continuous and discrete variables? If you are using eucledian distance as
a discrepancy measure you should try other option like using a Chi-square 2
association
statistic. I had a work where I had to deal with a data set containing
continuous, ordinal discrete and binary variables. The option of making
classes of continuous variables and, then transforming this new classes as
well as the classes of the ordinal discrete variables in dummy variables
causes information loss and it not recomended by Chatfield&Collins. So I
used the Chi-sq association statistic and it worked quite well.
Sorry if you are totally aware of this point, I just intend to be helpful.

> 2.  I have also found real differences between the outputs using the raw
(standardised) data set with all 96 variables and the 7 PCA factor scores -
looking at the cluster separation spatially in ArcView, the clustering with
the raw data makes much more sense.  Has anyone similar experience of
comparing raw and PCA summarised cluster analyses?

PCA is more a geometrical than 'statistical' approach. Besides other factor,
the distance measure you are using may influence a lot the results.

I believe I am not aiding in solving your problem but I hope this will give
any helpful hint.

All the best,
    Nuno

