> would cause this before I get too excited about my results?  As an
> aside, it would be nice to see the actual value regardless of the order
> of magnitude.  Thanks.

It's only printed to 4 dp:

> wilcox.test(1:24, (25:48)+0.1*rnorm(24), paired=T)

        Exact Wilcoxon signed-rank test

data:  1:24 and (25:48) + 0.1 * rnorm(24)
signed-rank statistic V = 0, n = 24, p-value = 0
alternative hypothesis: true mu is not equal to 0

so you wanted:

> wilcox.test(1:24, (25:48)+0.1*rnorm(24), paired=T)$p.value
[1] 1.192093e-007

Do remember that what is printed/summarized is pretty-printed.

print.htest has a default arg digits=4 (but it seems 4 is hard-coded).
Actually, I think print.htest should have printed 0.0000 for consistency,
so

        cat("p-value =", format(round(x$p.value, 4)), "\n")

should be

        cat("p-value =", format(round(x$p.value, digits), nsmall=digits), "\n")

