My pint of petrol for the fire.

I think it needs to be recognized that the EnvStats module was developed by 
a third party independent of Mathsoft/Insightful.  It was developed in 
response to environmental law in the US and offers a a package of 
statitistical and graphics functions specific to those regulations.  (There 
are approximately two pages of USEPA guidance documents in the reference 
section of the manual).  Althought it was designed specifically for those 
of us who deal with enviromental data, it certainly has capabilities others 
would find useful.

Yes, I am an unobjective observer.  The EnvStats module is why I use 
S-PLUS.  Given the cost of S-PLUS seminars, the help system alone (an 
online textbook of environmental stats) seems worth the cost of admission. 
(Disclaimer - I have not attended a S-PLUS seminar and am not commenting on 
those).  The EnvStats developer, Dr. Steve Millard, certainly deserves 
compensation for his efforts.  The price of the module for someone (or 
corporation) in this industry is a fair one, in my opinion.

I am not clear on the current relationship between Dr. Millard, his 
company, and Insightful, but I hope he is still getting a healthy piece of 
the EnvStats pie.

Now, about that Spatial Stats Module.....

